gned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x+1)+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3z)+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xy) \\\\  & =2+0+0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}2\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{5}2\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{5}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[2x]_{x=0}^{x=2}\\cdot (3-0)\\cdot (5-0) \\\\  & =(4-0)\\cdot 3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["b5c52282-8c13-5e43-82c0-823fefb3d635"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "c8b23a3e-7c17-526a-928a-85fad0743c35" :answer/id #uuid "c8b23a3e-7c17-526a-928a-85fad0743c35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-190" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "ebd986c9-62eb-5305-bc07-9934063ce422" :answer/id #uuid "ebd986c9-62eb-5305-bc07-9934063ce422" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{76}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "fb27b467-af9b-5a6d-96cb-01e4a3ca7ccb" :answer/id #uuid "fb27b467-af9b-5a6d-96cb-01e4a3ca7ccb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "95" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "f659541f-1b8a-5155-9cf3-659c2f25168c" :answer/id #uuid "f659541f-1b8a-5155-9cf3-659c2f25168c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "190" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "63c318c6-6247-51e3-89f5-9e01e2e02c28" :answer/id #uuid "63c318c6-6247-51e3-89f5-9e01e2e02c28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{190}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "1dbf10de-f8a4-595c-8a46-44ae442b863f" :answer-field/id #uuid "1dbf10de-f8a4-595c-8a46-44ae442b863f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["c8b23a3e-7c17-526a-928a-85fad0743c35" "ebd986c9-62eb-5305-bc07-9934063ce422" "fb27b467-af9b-5a6d-96cb-01e4a3ca7ccb" "f659541f-1b8a-5155-9cf3-659c2f25168c" "63c318c6-6247-51e3-89f5-9e01e2e02c28"] :answer-field/correct "f659541f-1b8a-5155-9cf3-659c2f25168c" :db/ensure :answer-field/validate} {:db/id "eb29068f-b574-5550-a633-ed4fe55ef0d6" :question/id #uuid "eb29068f-b574-5550-a633-ed4fe55ef0d6" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the boundary of the rectangular prism enclosed by the planes $x=2$, $x=3$, $y=2$, $y=3$, $z=2$, $z=4$. Given that the surface $S$ is positively (outward) oriented and $F={e}^{z}\\,i+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,j+4{x}^{2}yz\\,k$, find the flux of $F$ across $S$." :question/worked-solution "Let $R$ be a simple solid region bounded by a closed surface $S$ with positive (outward) orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4{x}^{2}yz) \\\\  & =0+2 x^{2} y+4 x^{2} y \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{2}^{3}{\\int }_{2}^{4}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{2}^{3}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{2}^{4}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}]_{x=2}^{x=3}\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=2}^{y=3}\\cdot (4-2) \\\\  & =(27-8)\\cdot (9-4)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =190.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["1dbf10de-f8a4-595c-8a46-44ae442b863f"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "ca848204-1be2-5069-9e32-ed8d35b33b43" :answer/id #uuid "ca848204-1be2-5069-9e32-ed8d35b33b43" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure :a