in an open region in space that contains $R,$ then the divergence theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∭}_{R}\\text{div}\\,F\\,\\text{d}V.\n$$\n\nComputing the divergence of $F,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{div}\\,F & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{z})+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}{y}^{2})+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(4{x}^{2}yz) \\\\  & =0+2 x^{2} y+4 x^{2} y \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $R$ be the solid region enclosed by $S.$ Then, using the divergence theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS & ={∭}_{R}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\cdot {\\int }_{1}^{4}2y\\,\\text{d}y\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}z \\\\  & =[{x}^{3}]_{x=2}^{x=4}\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=1}^{y=4}\\cdot (2-0) \\\\  & =(64-8)\\cdot (16-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =1680.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["97a800ab-9ed7-5211-b33b-dbc03e4af6ee"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "db42b8fd-128f-574b-a418-bc6e345e7388" :answer/id #uuid "db42b8fd-128f-574b-a418-bc6e345e7388" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-416" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "8d61fe98-57f2-508d-8d4a-f1a0ccc16cd8" :answer/id #uuid "8d61fe98-57f2-508d-8d4a-f1a0ccc16cd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{208}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "e308e49f-0fb4-5ca5-9e0e-32529b1c5871" :answer/id #uuid "e308e49f-0fb4-5ca5-9e0e-32529b1c5871" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "208" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "6cc3bf00-f3c4-575c-be10-687ff969f6c4" :answer/id #uuid "6cc3bf00-f3c4-575c-be10-687ff969f6c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "416" :db/ensure :answer/validate} {:db/id "3d11677f-b41e-53c2-82d6-2e3f223790cb" :answer/id #uuid "3d11677f-b41e-53c2-82d6-2e3f223790cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{416}{3}" :db/ensure :answer/validate}